.TH EXIT 2 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
exit \- terminate the calling process
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "void _exit(int " status ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B _exit()
terminates the calling process "immediately". Any open file descriptors belonging to the process are closed. The process's parent is sent a
.B SIGCHLD
signal.
.PP
The value
.I status
is returned to the parent process as the process's exit status, and can be collected using
.BR wait (2).
.SH RETURN VALUE
This function does not return.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro(2)
